Converts between time_t and struct tm with musl 1.2.5's calendar code
(ports/mlibc/musl/calendar.hpp): mlibc's counted 31 December as day 366
of every year (its day-of-year formula took every year for a leap
year), got times before 1970 wrong, and its mktime was timegm, which
neither used the time zone nor put fields in range or filled in tm_wday
and tm_yday. Also:
  - gmtime sets tm_isdst to 0, not -1, so strftime's %z works;
  - mktime uses the time zone and timelocal is mktime;
  - localtime falls back to UTC instead of ending the program when the
    time zone cannot be read;
  - the TZ rules' transition days come from the calendar (J60 is 1
    March in a leap year too) at their times of day, in UTC.
Meant for upstream.

